---
---

<section class="section invert noise" id="money">
	<div class="wrap">
		<span class="numeral" aria-hidden="true">04</span>

		<div class="head">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Revenue split</p>
				<h2>Sovereign payments, minimally extractive</h2>
			</div>
			<span class="split" aria-label="zero percent to Station, one hundred percent to you">
				<em>0%</em>
				<span class="bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<em>100%</em>
				<span class="split-key">station | you</span>
			</span>
		</div>

		<div class="body">
			<div class="col">
				<p class="lede">
					Station is launching with zero rev share. You keep all of your income. Only smart contract based finance models can provide this guarantee.
				</p>
				<p>
					All payments are routed through smart contracts that
					<strong>you</strong> deploy and <strong>you</strong> own.
					The payment split logic is baked into your contracts and can't be modified by anyone, ever.
					There's no invoice, no billing cycle, and no moment where we hold your money and pass some of it back.
				</p>
				<p>
					Station can increase this rev share rate in the future for later adopters in order to grow the
					services over time, but artists rates are locked in at a cryptographically guaranteed level,
					rather than a platform promise that we're trying to sell you on.
					The smart contract infrastructure is what lets us find a balance between providing a minimally
					extractive solution for artists that favors the early adopters and paves a path for Station to 
					grow and expand services over time.
					Whatever your split was on the day you deployed is the split it keeps,
					permanently.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="col">
				<blockquote>
					The protection isn't that we promise not to raise your rate. It's that we can't.
				</blockquote>

				<p class="aside">
					A streaming platform sets its terms in an agreement and reserves the right to revise it.
					There's no recourse because there's nothing to enforce — the terms live on their side of
					the relationship, and so does the ability to rewrite them.
				</p>
				<p class="aside">
					The first increase, whenever it arrives, will be 1% | 99%, and it will apply only to
					contracts deployed after it. There is no rev share increase schedule; we're gonna play it by ear.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	/* Hard-cut inversion — the one section that looks nothing like the rest. */
	.invert {
		background: var(--white);
		color: var(--black);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--black);
	}

	.invert .numeral {
		-webkit-text-stroke: 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
	}

	.invert .eyebrow {
		color: #1c7f3e;
	}

	.head {
		display: flex;
		align-items: flex-end;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 2rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		padding-bottom: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--black);
	}

	.split {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.7rem;
		position: relative;
		padding-bottom: 1.4rem;
		transform: rotate(-1deg);
	}

	.split em {
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-style: normal;
		font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4rem);
		line-height: 0.85;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.split em:last-of-type {
		color: #158a3f;
	}

	.bar {
		width: 1px;
		height: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
		background: var(--black);
	}

	.split-key {
		position: absolute;
		bottom: 0;
		left: 0;
		font-size: 0.62rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.2em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
	}

	.body {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(19rem, 1fr));
		gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}

	.col p + p {
		margin-top: 1.1rem;
	}

	.body p {
		color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.82);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
	}

	.body .lede {
		font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.94rem + 0.32vw, 1.2rem);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--black);
	}

	.body strong {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--black);
	}

	blockquote {
		font-family: var(--display);
		font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 2.4rem);
		line-height: 1.02;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		border-left: 4px solid #158a3f;
		padding-left: clamp(0.9rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
		margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
		max-width: 22ch;
	}

	.aside {
		max-width: 46ch;
	}

	.aside + .aside {
		margin-top: 1.1rem;
	}
</style>
